.TH SPACE-NERDS-IN-SPACE "6" "October 2026" "snis_web_gateway" "Games"
.SH NAME
snis_web_gateway \- HTTP/HTTPS server and WebSocket-to-TCP relay for the Space Nerds In Space web client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snis_web_gateway
[
.B \-p
.I port
] [
.B \-r
.I directory
] [
.B \-a
.I host:port
] [
.B \-l
.I lobbyhost
] [
.B \-c
.I certfile
.B \-k
.I keyfile
] [
.B \-n
] [
.B \-v
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.warn 511
.PP
snis_web_gateway provides everything a web browser needs to run the browser
build of snis_client on a single port:
.PP
It serves the browser client's files (by default from \fBbin/web\fR, built by
"make WEB=1 web"), including the Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy and
Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy HTTP headers that browsers require before allowing
threads (SharedArrayBuffer).
.PP
It relays WebSockets to TCP connections, because a browser cannot open a raw
TCP connection directly to snis_server or ssgl_server.  When the web client
requests \fB/relay/\fIhost\fB/\fIport\fR, the gateway connects to that host and
port over TCP and passes bytes in both directions.  It relays only to addresses
it has been explicitly told to allow: those specified with \fB\-\-allow\fR, the
lobby server specified with \fB\-\-lobby\fR, and every game server listed by
that lobby.
.PP
It speaks both HTTP and HTTPS on the same port, distinguishing them by
inspecting the first byte sent by the client.  Browsers allow threads only in a
"secure context" (such as \fBhttp://localhost\fR or an \fBhttps://\fR URL), so
players connecting from other machines must use HTTPS.  Unless given a
certificate and private key via \fB\-\-cert\fR and \fB\-\-key\fR (or disabled
with \fB\-\-no\-tls\fR), the gateway automatically generates a self-signed
certificate naming the local machine and its IPv4 addresses the first time it
runs.
.PP
Nothing in snis_server, snis_multiverse, or ssgl_server needs to know about
snis_web_gateway; to them, a browser connecting through the gateway is a client
like any other.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p, \-\-port \fIport\fR
Port to listen on for both HTTP and HTTPS connections (default 8088).
.TP
\fB\-r, \-\-root \fIdirectory\fR
Document root directory to serve files from (default \fBbin/web\fR).  A request
for \fB/\fR serves \fB/snis_client.html\fR.
.TP
\fB\-a, \-\-allow \fIhost:port\fR
Allow browsers to relay connections to the snis_server at \fIhost:port\fR.
This option may be repeated to allow multiple servers.
.TP
\fB\-l, \-\-lobby \fIhost\fR
Allow browsers to relay connections to the ssgl_server lobby at \fIhost\fR
(with an optional \fI:port\fR suffix) and to every SNIS game server listed by
that lobby.  The gateway polls the lobby every 5 seconds to keep its allowlist
updated.
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-cert \fIfile\fR
Use the PEM certificate chain in \fIfile\fR for HTTPS instead of generating or
using the default self-signed certificate.  Must be used together with
\fB\-\-key\fR.
.TP
\fB\-k, \-\-key \fIfile\fR
Use the PEM private key in \fIfile\fR for HTTPS.  Must be used together with
\fB\-\-cert\fR.
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-no\-tls\fR
Serve HTTP only and do not set up TLS/HTTPS.  This is sufficient when the
browser is running on the same machine as the gateway (\fBhttp://localhost\fR).
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Print additional diagnostic messages to standard error, including allowed relay
addresses, HTTP requests, and TLS handshake failures.
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print a usage message and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
For a bare snis_server started without a lobby on port 2501:
.nf

	snis_server --nolobby --port 2501 -L x
	snis_web_gateway --allow localhost:2501
.fi
.PP
Then open \fBhttp://localhost:8088/\fR on the same machine, or
\fBhttps://<hostname>:8088/\fR from another machine on the network.
.PP
To allow connections to a lobby server and all game servers registered with it:
.nf

	snis_web_gateway --lobby localhost
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
\fBbin/web\fR
Default document root directory containing \fBsnis_client.html\fR,
\fBsnis_client.js\fR, \fBsnis_client.wasm\fR, and \fBsnis_client.data\fR.
.TP
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/space-nerds-in-space/web-gateway-cert.pem\fR,
.TP
\fB$HOME/.local/share/space-nerds-in-space/web-gateway-cert.pem\fR
Default path where the auto-generated self-signed X.509 certificate is stored.
.TP
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/space-nerds-in-space/web-gateway-key.pem\fR,
.TP
\fB$HOME/.local/share/space-nerds-in-space/web-gateway-key.pem\fR
Default path where the auto-generated private key is stored.  If the machine's
IP addresses or hostname change, delete both \fB.pem\fR files so that
snis_web_gateway generates a new certificate on its next startup.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
\fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR
If set, the auto-generated certificate and private key are stored in
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/space-nerds-in-space/\fR instead of
\fB$HOME/.local/share/space-nerds-in-space/\fR.
.TP
\fBHOME\fR
Used to locate \fB.local/share/space-nerds-in-space/\fR when
\fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR is not set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
snis_client(6), snis_server(6), snis_multiverse(6), ssgl_server(6)
.br
